<Publish>
	<!--This PublishConfiguration.xml file is required to publish a mod on Paradox website and is part of the CSII toolchain-->
	
	<!-- Id must be set in order to update existing mod; not required for publishing mod for the first time -->
	<ModId Value="136261" />

	<!-- Display name -->
	<DisplayName Value="Easy Zoning [EZ]" />

	<!-- Short one-liner -->
	<ShortDescription Value="Change road Zoning: Both/Left/Right/None. RMB cycles, LMB applies." />

	<!-- Long description (minimal markdown supported) -->
	<LongDescription>
        # Easy Zoning [EZ] Beta

        Custom zoning for new and existing roads.

        ## How to use

        **New Road:**
        1. Open Roads panel (i.e., pick small roads)
        2. Near the bottom of the road tool panel, pick one of 3 EZ icons (see image).
        3. Draw as usual (road appears with cells on one side or no-sides if the 3 icons are flipped off).

        **Existing Road:**
        1. Open EZ Update panel: Ctrl+Z toggles panel on/off (top-left icon does the same).
        2. Select an icon to pick a zone side (see image).
        3. Hover a road to preview.
        4. Right-Click road to switch sides (infinitely); **RMB cycles** Both → Left → Right → None →...
        5. Left-Click (LMB) to apply (lock it in).
        6. Or LMB hold+drag along many road sections, release and update is applied.
        7. If the road has a blue color outline, then it's a candidate for the update; if no color, then there is no change (it already has zoning on that side).

        ## Features
        - **Contour Lines** terrain toggle
        - Highlight outline blue color indicates the road did not get the change yet.

        Options Menu
        - ✅ Protect occupied cells (buildings).
        - ✅ Protect zoned-but-empty cells.
        - ✅ Default **Ctrl +Z** short-cut can be changed (it opens/closes EZ panel fast)
        - ✅ **Legacy RMB mode** (optional): RMB toggles **Left↔Right** and **Both↔None** instead of all 4-states

        ## Compatibility
        - Remove Zone Tools or ART mod to avoid conflicts.
        - No Harmony, extends vanilla UI (helps it be more stable on game patch days and increases compatibility).
        - Safe to remove any time. Road you zoned will keep their zoning.
        - Should work with Platter mod.
        - Lightweight, optimized, runs only when needed.

        ## Support and feedback
        - If mod helps you, give it a Like, it's free + easy :)
        - Feedback to GitHub, Discord, or forum links on this page.

        ## Tech notes
        For newly drawn roads, “Left/Right” is relative to the segment’s orientation.
        At some diagonal angles  (↖||↗) it may apply flipped from what you want — use RMB to swap.


        ## Credits

        - River-mochi - author
        - thanks to Kemorno (original ART mod, retired) and zeeshanabid 94 (zoning toolkit, retired)
        - yenyang - technical support and encouragement
        - Rouchesta - testing
        - CS2 modding community for testing, feedback


    </LongDescription>
	
